>> title: Luncheon Meat and Egg Sandwich
>> category: Sandwiches & Rolls
>> tags: luncheon meat, eggs, sandwich, bread, hong kong, quick
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: chaan daan ji, 餐蛋治, 蛋牛治, Spam & Egg Sandwich, spam and egg sandwich, luncheon meat and egg sandwich, corn beef & egg sandwich
>> servings: 1
>> time: 12 min
>> step.1: fry the slices 4 min, both faces browned
>> step.2: fold an omelette 2 min, no colour on it
>> step.3: toast and butter, 2 min
>> step.4: stack meat under egg, cut it in half

Fry @tinned luncheon meat{3%slices}(1/4-in thick) in @neutral oil{2%tsp} in a #frying pan{} for ~fry{4%min}, turning once, until both faces have browned.

Beat @eggs{2%large} with @fine salt{1/4%tsp} and @white pepper{1/8%tsp}, pour them into a #nonstick pan{}, and fold them into a flat omelette over ~fry{2%min} without letting it take colour.

Toast @white sandwich bread{2%slices} for ~toast{2%min} and spread @salted butter{2%tsp}(softened) over both inside faces.

Stack @&(~3)luncheon meat{} under @&(~2)omelette{} between @&(~1)toast{}, press the lid down, and cut it in half.
